# AIMemory Agents

## Alias policy

Agent selectors use `<agent>[:<model-or-tier>[:<profile>]]`.

If only an agent name is provided, the orchestrator chooses the model/profile
by task difficulty and records the choice in the goal record.

## Default orchestration policy

- default_policy: single_agent
- verifier_required: user_selectable
- headless_requires_explicit_awm: true
- goal_auto_run_default: true
- goal_cursor_file: AIMemory/goals/ACTIVE.md
- goal_ledger_file: AIMemory/goals/INDEX.md
- completion_guard_required: true
- telemetry_policy: compact_only
- agent_call_probe: lazy
- agent_registration: natural_language_aliases

## Model and profile policy

- model_or_tier labels are project-safe routing labels such as `auto`, `pro`,
  `max`, `local`, or a public model name.
- profile labels describe effort, context, or tool policy such as `auto`,
  `standard`, `max`, or `readonly`.
- Private executable paths, account names, provider credentials, and machine
  paths never appear here.

## Project aliases
| Alias | Resolves to | Capabilities | Notes |
|-------|-------------|--------------|-------|
| claude | claude:auto:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Guarded CLI: live dispatch requires an explicit user request. |
| claude-max | claude:opus-4.7:max | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec, subagent-spawn | Expensive/high-context profile. |
| codex | codex:gpt-5-codex:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Guarded CLI: live dispatch requires an explicit user request. |
| opencode | opencode:auto:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Run `/awm agents test opencode --smoke` before dispatch. |
| opencode-deepseek | opencode:deepseek:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Registered from `/awm agents add 오픈코드의 딥시크`; run `/awm agents test opencode-deepseek --smoke` before dispatch. |
| 딥시크 | opencode:deepseek:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Registered from `/awm agent add 딥시크 오픈코드:딥시크` or `/awm agent add 딥시크 오픈코드의 딥시크`; run `/awm agents test 딥시크 --smoke` before dispatch. |
| continue-deepseek | continue:deepseek:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Continue CLI `cn` supports headless JSON, `cn serve`, and `--readonly`; run `/awm agents test continue-deepseek --smoke` before dispatch. |
| aider-deepseek | aider:deepseek:auto | filesystem-read, filesystem-write, shell-exec | Aider supports headless `--message`; run `/awm agents test aider-deepseek --smoke` before dispatch. |
| gemini-pro | gemini:pro:auto | filesystem-read, web-search, image-input | Use when multimodal or long-context search is needed. |

## Agent registration notes

- `/awm agents add <description>` appends safe project-scoped aliases.
- Natural-language examples such as `오픈코드의 딥시크` are normalized to ASCII
  alias/selector rows such as `opencode-deepseek -> opencode:deepseek:auto`.
- `/awm agent add <alias> <selector-or-description>` uses the first argument as
  the alias, so both `딥시크 오픈코드:딥시크` and `딥시크 오픈코드의 딥시크`
  register `딥시크 -> opencode:deepseek:auto`.
- Use `--as` to choose the alias in plural form and `--selector` to force the
  exact selector.
- Registered aliases are untested until `/awm agents test <alias> --smoke`
  updates `Agent call hints`.

## Private overrides

Private executable paths, account names, credentials, tokens, and local config
belong in ignored `.agent-work-mux/agents.local.md` or environment variables.
Do not add them here.

## Agent call hints
| Agent | Last tested | CLI/version | Headless status | Invocation hint | Telemetry | Known quirks |
|-------|-------------|-------------|-----------------|-----------------|-----------|--------------|
| opencode | 2026-05-08 | opencode 1.14.33 | pass | `opencode run --model deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash --format json "<prompt>"` | JSON events include `step_finish` tokens/cost | Put message before repeated `--file` args. |
| continue | 2026-05-08 | Continue CLI 1.5.45 | pass | `cn [--config <config-if-needed>] --readonly -p "<prompt>" --format json` | JSON output in headless mode; `cn serve --port <port>` `/state` passed | Any working Continue secret setup is valid; local env fallback needed explicit `apiKey: ${{ secrets.//DEEPSEEK_API_KEY }}` on this probe. |
| codex | 2026-05-08 | codex-cli 0.128.0 | guarded_check_only | default: `codex --version`; live on request: `codex exec --ephemeral --json --output-last-message <file> --cd <project> "<prompt>"` | Default probe collects no token telemetry; live runs emit JSONL `turn.completed` usage. | Guarded CLI: require explicit user request or `--live`. |
| gemini | 2026-05-08 | gemini-cli 0.41.2 | guarded_check_only | default: `gemini --version`; live on request: `gemini --prompt "<prompt>" --approval-mode plan --output-format json --skip-trust` | Default probe collects no token telemetry; live runs emit JSON stats. | Guarded CLI, especially from Antigravity/Gemini contexts: require explicit user request or `--live`. |
| aider | 2026-05-08 | aider 0.86.2 | pass | `aider --model deepseek/deepseek-chat --message "<prompt>" --no-git --no-auto-commits --no-stream --no-pretty --yes-always --no-analytics --input-history-file .agent-work-mux/tmp/aider/input.history --chat-history-file .agent-work-mux/tmp/aider/chat.history.md --llm-history-file .agent-work-mux/tmp/aider/llm.history` | stdout includes tokens/cost | Include "Do not edit files" in smoke prompts; redirect history files to ignored local state. |
| antigravity | 2026-05-08 | Antigravity 1.107.0 | gui_only | `antigravity chat --mode ask "<prompt>"` | none | Opens/targets GUI chat and returned no machine-readable result. |
| cursor | 2026-05-08 | Cursor 3.3.22 | gui_only | `<Cursor install>/resources/app/bin/cursor.cmd --chat` | none | Editor/chat launcher only; may not be on PATH. |
| claude | 2026-05-08 | Claude Code 2.1.132 | guarded_check_only | default: `claude --version` and auth status; live on request: `claude -p "<prompt>" --output-format json --permission-mode plan --no-session-persistence` | Default probe collects auth/version only; live runs can emit JSON usage/error metadata. | Guarded CLI: require explicit user request or `--live`. |
